Usage: vcpe diagnose --from <service> --to <webpa|webhook|callback> [flags]

Shows a bounded diagnostic graph and its first confirmed failure through persisted loopback endpoints. Use --to webpa with --client-service for CPE diagnostics, --to webhook for registration inspection, or --to callback for one bounded CPE-to-subscriber event after explicit active-event consent.

Required flags:
  --from <service>        Source service name
  --to <webpa|webhook|callback>  Diagnostic target journey

Optional flags:
  --name <deployment>     Deployment containing the source and WebPA services; optional when exactly one deployment is active
  --client-service <name>  Required for --to webpa and --to callback; receive-enabled libparodus service
  --subscriber <service>  Required for --to callback; selected event-sink subscriber
  --allow-active-callback  Generate one direct callback and one synthetic Caduceus event for --to webhook
  --allow-active-event    Required for --to callback; permit one bounded CPE-generated diagnostic event
  --event <destination>   Required with active webhook diagnosis; representative event destination
  --device-id <identity>  Required with active webhook diagnosis; representative device identity
  --replica <index>       Zero-based source replica index; required when replicas exceed one
  --subscriber-replica <index>  Selected subscriber replica for --to callback when replicas exceed one
  --state-root <path>     Override the default state root directory
  --json                  Emit the vcpe.dev/diagnostic/v1 graph

Examples:
  vcpe diagnose --from gateway --to webpa --client-service apparmor-simulator
  vcpe diagnose --name example --from event-sink --to webhook
  vcpe diagnose --name example --from event-sink --to webhook --allow-active-callback --event devices/diagnostic --device-id mac:001122334455
  vcpe diagnose --name example --from gateway --to callback --client-service apparmor-simulator --subscriber event-sink --allow-active-event --event devices/diagnostic --device-id mac:001122334455
